=begin pod

=TITLE App::FontSample

=SUBTITLE Produce PDF font specimens from any C<PDF::Content::FontObj>

=head1 SYNOPSIS

Library use with one already-loaded font:

=begin code :lang<raku>
use App::FontSample;

create-font-sample(
    $font,
    :name<MyFont-Regular>,
    :paper<Letter>,
    :layout<specimen>,
    :output<my-font.pdf>,
);
=end code

Command-line use with an OTF or TTF file:

=begin code :lang<text>
font-sample \
    --font=/path/to/font.otf \
    --output=sample.pdf \
    --layout=specimen \
    --paper=Letter
=end code

A reproducible JSON definition can contain one sample or several jobs:

=begin code :lang<text>
font-sample --config=font-samples.json
=end code

=head1 DESCRIPTION

C<App::FontSample> separates font acquisition from PDF specimen rendering.
Library callers supply one or more already-loaded C<PDF::Content::FontObj>
objects. The installed C<font-sample> program can load OTF or TTF files
directly or read JSON job definitions.

The library is provider-neutral. C<NotoFonts-OT> is useful with the examples,
but it is not a dependency of C<App::FontSample>.

Letter and A4 paper are supported in portrait and landscape orientation.
Margins are expressed in PDF points; 72 points equal one inch.

=head1 LAYOUTS

=head2 specimen

One page per font. Shows the font name, uppercase and lowercase alphabets,
numerals and punctuation, a pangram, and a size waterfall.

=head2 waterfall

Accepted as a specimen-compatible layout. The specimen page includes a size
waterfall controlled by the C<sizes> option. A dedicated waterfall-only page
is listed in the TODO section.

=head2 comparison

Shows the same sample text in each supplied font. Rows are automatically
continued onto additional pages when necessary. C<comparison-size> controls
the sample size and defaults to 18 points.

=head2 collection

Places a compact font collection on one page. C<sample-size> defaults to 14
points and C<leading-ratio> defaults to 0.20. The layout refuses to overflow
the lower margin; use C<comparison> when the font set does not fit.

=head2 characters

Shows selected characters in a grid with a C<U+XXXX> label beneath each glyph.
The grid automatically continues onto additional pages. C<columns> defaults
to 8. Library callers may also pass C<glyph-size>.

=head1 LIBRARY API

=head2 create-font-sample

Creates a PDF from one C<PDF::Content::FontObj>.

=head2 create-font-collection-sample

Creates a PDF from a non-empty collection of C<App::FontSample::FontEntry>
objects. The default collection layout is C<comparison>.

=head1 NOTOFONTS-OT EXAMPLE

C<NotoFonts-OT> exports C<get-loaded-font>, so it can be used without a
provider object:

=begin code :lang<raku>
use NotoFonts-OT;
use App::FontSample;
use App::FontSample::FontEntry;

my @entries;

for <
    NotoSerif-Regular
    NotoSerif-Bold
    NotoSans-Regular
    NotoSans-Bold
> -> $code {
    my $font = get-loaded-font($code);

    @entries.push: App::FontSample::FontEntry.new(
        :name($code),
        :$font,
    );
}

create-font-collection-sample(
    @entries,
    :layout<comparison>,
    :output<noto-comparison.pdf>,
);
=end code

=head1 COMMAND-LINE PROGRAM

Direct mode requires C<--font> and C<--output>. Important options include:

=item C<--layout=specimen|waterfall|comparison|characters|collection>
=item C<--paper=Letter|A4>
=item C<--landscape>
=item C<--margin=POINTS>
=item C<--language=CODE>
=item C<--text=TEXT>
=item C<--pangram=TEXT>
=item C<--sizes=N,N,...>
=item C<--characters=TEXT>
=item C<--columns=N>
=item C<--comparison-size=N>
=item C<--sample-size=N>
=item C<--leading-ratio=N>
=item C<--languages>

=head1 JSON INPUT

The original single-job object remains valid:

=begin code :lang<json>
{
    "output": "output/sample.pdf",
    "layout": "specimen",
    "fonts": [
        {
            "file": "fonts/MyFont.otf",
            "name": "My Font"
        }
    ]
}
=end code

For several related outputs, use C<defaults> plus C<samples>:

=begin code :lang<json>
{
    "defaults": {
        "paper": "Letter",
        "margin": 36,
        "fonts": [
            {
                "file": "fonts/MyFont-Regular.otf",
                "name": "MyFont Regular"
            },
            {
                "file": "fonts/MyFont-Bold.otf",
                "name": "MyFont Bold"
            }
        ]
    },
    "samples": [
        {
            "output": "output/comparison.pdf",
            "layout": "comparison",
            "comparison-size": 18
        },
        {
            "output": "output/characters.pdf",
            "layout": "characters",
            "characters": "ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ0123456789",
            "columns": 8
        }
    ]
}
=end code

Sample values override values in C<defaults>. Relative font and output paths
are interpreted relative to the JSON definition file, not the current working
directory.

=head1 LANGUAGE SAMPLES

C<App::FontSample::SampleText> provides a small built-in pangram registry.
List the available language codes with:

=begin code :lang<text>
font-sample --languages
=end code

A library caller may register additional sample text at runtime.

=head1 TESTING

Run the normal test suite with:

=begin code :lang<text>
zef test .
=end code

Visual examples that depend on C<NotoFonts-OT> should remain outside the
normal dependency path so the application continues to work with any suitable
font source.

=head1 TODO

The current release is intended to be useful as-is. Planned improvements are:

=item Add a dedicated waterfall-only renderer instead of using the specimen
renderer for C<waterfall>.

=item Add optional character-cell borders, baseline/cap-height guides, and
small edge tick marks for font-metric inspection.

=item Extend C<characters> input with convenient Unicode range notation such
as C<0020..007E> and named blocks.

=item Add more tests that emulate the installed command-line examples,
including multi-page comparison and character output.

=item Expand the built-in language sample registry and document which fonts
cover each sample.

=item Add more polished JSON examples for specimen, comparison, collection,
and character-grid jobs.

=item Review whether the obsolete C<App::FontSample::Provider> role should be
removed in a later API cleanup.

=item Consider a separate helper for discovering or installing additional
Noto fonts; keep that functionality outside the provider-neutral core.

=head1 AUTHOR

Thomas Browder

=end pod
